package com.sliverzfx.gothicquest

object NewBalanceChapter1Part1 {
    val quests = listOf(
        Quest("CH1-001",1,1,"The Eye of Innos",category="Main Story",giver = "Xardas",location="Main Story",prerequisites="Main story; begins in Chapter 1.",summary="Xardas sends you to Khorinis to obtain the Eye of Innos.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Xardas sends you to Khorinis to obtain the Eye of Innos. Gain access to the Upper Quarter and Town Hall, join a main guild, speak with Lord Hagen, then complete the Water Mages, The Portal's Secret and Evidence questlines. In Chapter 3 follow the trail of the stolen Eye from Pyrokar toward the Sun Circle, recover the broken amulet, arrange Bennet's release so he can repair it, and convince Vatras, Pyrokar and Xardas to perform the restoration ritual at the Sun Circle. Bring 3 swampweed stalks and collect the repaired Eye from Bennet before the ritual."),reward="Multiple staged XP rewards; completing the ritual restores the Eye and begins Dragon Hunt.",warnings="If you reached the Valley of Mines before Jharkendar, Vatras will not advance the Eye quest until Raven is completed. Militia must become paladins and mercenaries must become dragon hunters before Xardas agrees to the ritual; other main guilds can proceed immediately.",searchTags=listOf("the eye of innos","main story","xardas")),
        Quest("CH1-002",1,2,"Access to the Upper Quarter",category="Main Story",giver = "Rupert",location="Main Story",prerequisites="Guildless when the quest is offered.",summary="Become a citizen by completing Masters' Trust and then The Path to Apprenticeship in Khorinis, or join a main guild and complete that guild's access requirement.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Become a citizen by completing Masters' Trust and then The Path to Apprenticeship in Khorinis, or join a main guild and complete that guild's access requirement. Once you are legitimately allowed into the Upper Quarter, speak to the guard at its entrance to finish the quest."),reward="500 XP on legitimate completion.",warnings="Each guild has a different route to Town Hall access. A temporary exploit allows climbing from an empty market stall to the Upper Quarter balcony, but guards will raise the alarm during the day if you are not authorized.",searchTags=listOf("access to the upper quarter","main story","rupert")),
        Quest("CH1-003",1,3,"The Water Mages",category="Main Story",giver = "Saturas, Cavalorn or Vatras",location="Main Story",prerequisites="Can be journal-started by Saturas; full progress requires The Ring of Water.",summary="After helping Cavalorn with the nearby bandits, take his letter to Vatras and say it came from Cavalorn, then report back to Cavalorn.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("After helping Cavalorn with the nearby bandits, take his letter to Vatras and say it came from Cavalorn, then report back to Cavalorn. Begin The Ring of Water and investigate the missing people. When Vatras is satisfied, take the ornament fragment to Saturas at the excavation and continue the portal investigation with the Water Mages."),reward="Several staged XP awards, including 200 XP for delivering Cavalorn's letter and 200 XP for reporting back.",warnings="Talking to Saturas too early only creates the journal entry; he will send you away until the Ring of Water chain is active.",searchTags=listOf("the water mages","main story","saturas, cavalorn or vatras")),
        Quest("CH1-004",1,4,"The Ring of Water",category="Main Story",giver = "Cavalorn",location="Main Story",prerequisites="Ask Cavalorn about his armor.",summary="Cavalorn reveals the Ring of Water and sends you to Vatras.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Cavalorn reveals the Ring of Water and sends you to Vatras. Ask Vatras to join; he requires proof of your usefulness. Complete Where Are All the Missing People? and report the result. Follow Vatras' instructions to the Ring meeting at the Dead Harpy tavern, speak with Orlan/Lares as required, attend the initiation and receive the Ring equipment. Continue by taking Vatras' message/ornament business to Saturas."),reward="Ring of Water equipment and staged XP; additional XP is available for returning Lares' aquamarine ring when appropriate.",warnings="The missing-people investigation is the key gate; do not rush directly to the excavation expecting Saturas to accept you.",searchTags=listOf("the ring of water","main story","cavalorn")),
        Quest("CH1-005",1,5,"Where Are All the Missing People?",category="Main Story",giver = "Lothar or Vatras",location="Main Story",prerequisites="Chapter 1; central prerequisite for the Ring of Water.",summary="Start at Cardiff in the harbor tavern.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Start at Cardiff in the harbor tavern. Follow the witness chain: Cardiff points toward Halvor and Coragon; Coragon sends you to Hakon and Thorben; Halvor points toward Garvell and Farim; Farim finally directs you to the beach north of Khorinis. Continue the clues until you identify the bandit/slave-trader operation and Dexter's involvement, then report the case to Vatras."),reward="Progresses Ring of Water/main story; staged XP from discoveries and reports.",warnings="Following every witness is worthwhile because several side quests and missing-person entries are opened during the investigation.",searchTags=listOf("where are all the missing people?","main story","lothar or vatras")),
        Quest("CH1-006",1,6,"The Portal",category="Main Story",giver = "Nefarius",location="Main Story",prerequisites="Begins automatically when you activate your first stone circle, or through Nefarius.",summary="Activate the three stone circles by pressing the three pillar buttons around each circle.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Activate the three stone circles by pressing the three pillar buttons around each circle. Defeat the stone guardians that appear and take the ornament fragments. After advancing The Water Mages and bringing Vatras' ornament fragment to Saturas, speak with Nefarius, collect the remaining pieces and have the Water Mages restore the ornament so the portal can be opened."),reward="Unlocks the portal/Jharkendar progression and grants staged XP.",warnings="A stone guardian does not appear at the circle behind Lobart's farm. Activating circles early is allowed, but the quest cannot fully advance until the Water Mages chain reaches the excavation.",searchTags=listOf("the portal","main story","automatic / nefarius")),
        Quest("CH1-007",1,7,"Rune Stones",category="Xardas's Tower",giver = "Xardas",location="Xardas's Tower",prerequisites="Chapter 1; begins after leaving Xardas's tower and discovering the first druid rune stone.",summary="Inspect the first ancient rune stone you encounter after leaving Xardas's tower, then return to Xardas and ask about it.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Inspect the first ancient rune stone you encounter after leaving Xardas's tower, then return to Xardas and ask about it. He gives you a special teleport rune connected to the old network. Continue exploring Khorinis and activate the ancient rune tablets/stones scattered around the island; each one expands the network of usable teleport points."),reward="Access to the rune-stone teleport network and staged experience.",warnings="Activate rune stones whenever you find them. The network becomes one of the fastest ways to move around the enlarged New Balance world.",searchTags=listOf("rune stones","xardas's tower","automatic / xardas")),
        Quest("CH1-008",1,8,"Archmage",category="Xardas's Tower",giver = "Trigger quest",location="Xardas's Tower",prerequisites="Chapter 1; examine Xardas's bookshelves.",summary="Read the book in Xardas's library that mentions the demon language known as Leng.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Read the book in Xardas's library that mentions the demon language known as Leng. Ask Xardas about becoming an archmage and about the language. If he cannot teach the required knowledge directly, seek the necromancer Kreol, who can teach the demon language and continue the magical progression tied to this quest."),reward="Unlocks further magical study and demon-language related progression.",warnings="This is chiefly a magic/knowledge progression quest; do not ignore unique books in Xardas's tower.",searchTags=listOf("archmage","xardas's tower","automatic after reading a book in xardas's library")),
        Quest("CH1-009",1,9,"Northern Dark for Lester",category="Xardas's Tower",giver = "Lester",location="Xardas's Tower",prerequisites="Chapter 1; speak with Lester at night before Chapter 3.",summary="Talk to Lester at night.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Talk to Lester at night. He asks for a special 'Northern Dark' swampweed joint. Travel to the Brotherhood camp and locate the locked chest belonging to Guru Oran; the special joint is inside. Bring it back to Lester."),reward="500 XP and a King's Sorrel.",warnings="Finish this before Chapter 3, when Lester's situation changes.",searchTags=listOf("northern dark for lester","xardas's tower","lester")),
        Quest("CH1-010",1,10,"Soul Crystals",category="Xardas's Tower",giver = "Xardas",location="Xardas's Tower",prerequisites="Chapter 1; access to demon-related enemies and later New Balance areas.",summary="Collect Dark Soul Crystals from demonicons, named demons and other powerful demonic enemies throughout the game, including later areas such as the Ancient Plateau.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Collect Dark Soul Crystals from demonicons, named demons and other powerful demonic enemies throughout the game, including later areas such as the Ancient Plateau. Bring a set of 10 crystals to Xardas for the main turn-in. Check his dialogue again later after collecting more, because the quest has an additional reward stage."),reward="10 crystals: 3,000 XP. A later turn-in can award 1,000 XP and a Dark Soul elixir (+10 HP and +10 mana).",warnings="Do not sell or discard Dark Soul Crystals; they are quest currency.",searchTags=listOf("soul crystals","xardas's tower","xardas")),
        Quest("CH1-011",1,11,"The Road to Khorinis",category="Lobart's Farm",giver = "Maleth or Canthar",location="Lobart's Farm",prerequisites="Chapter 1; guildless on the road to Khorinis.",summary="Reach Khorinis by one of several routes.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Reach Khorinis by one of several routes. The intended early route is to work for Lobart, buy his farmer clothes at a reduced price, and tell the south-gate guards that you are going from Lobart to the blacksmith. Canthar can instead give you a pass in return for a later favor if you meet him before entering the city while dressed in rags/miner clothing/Brotherhood clothing. You can also pay the gate guards, wear sufficiently respectable armor, complete Herbs for Constantino, or swim around the eastern wall. After entering, speak with Lothar."),reward="Entry to Khorinis; route-dependent XP, rhetoric and/or Dexterity bonuses.",warnings="If you want Canthar's Favor, speak to Canthar under the correct conditions before entering the city. The swimming route can award an extra Lares bonus; you can then leave and re-enter through the south gate using the herb route for the rhetoric bonus.",searchTags=listOf("the road to khorinis","lobart's farm","maleth or canthar")),
        Quest("CH1-012",1,12,"Lobart's Work Clothes",category="Lobart's Farm",giver = "Lobart",location="Lobart's Farm",prerequisites="Chapter 1; speak with Lobart at his farm.",summary="Ask Lobart for work clothes.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Ask Lobart for work clothes. The starting price is high, but you can reduce it by siding with the farmers in dialogue and by completing the farm's small jobs: Harvesting Turnips, Turnips for Hilda, Frying Pan for Hilda, A Bottle of Wine, and Bandits Near Lobart's Farm. Return to Lobart after each job, then buy the clothes at the reduced price."),reward="Lobart's work clothes; price can be reduced from 80 gold to 30 gold.",warnings="Choosing dialogue supportive of the farmers gives a rhetoric bonus and lowers the price. Doing the side jobs is the cheapest route.",searchTags=listOf("lobart's work clothes","lobart's farm","lobart")),
        Quest("CH1-013",1,13,"Harvesting Turnips",category="Lobart's Farm",giver = "Lobart",location="Lobart's Farm",prerequisites="Chapter 1.",summary="Go to the turnip field beside Lobart's barn and collect the turnips growing there.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Go to the turnip field beside Lobart's barn and collect the turnips growing there. Return to Lobart and hand over the harvest."),reward="100 XP and either 5 gold or a 10-gold clothing discount.",warnings="You can take a small gold payment or use the job to reduce the price of Lobart's work clothes.",searchTags=listOf("harvesting turnips","lobart's farm","lobart")),
        Quest("CH1-014",1,14,"Turnips for Hilda",category="Lobart's Farm",giver = "Lobart / Hilda",location="Lobart's Farm",prerequisites="Complete Harvesting Turnips.",summary="After finishing the harvest, Lobart asks you to take the collected turnips to Hilda.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("After finishing the harvest, Lobart asks you to take the collected turnips to Hilda. Enter the farmhouse, speak with Hilda and hand them over."),reward="100 XP.",warnings="None of consequence.",searchTags=listOf("turnips for hilda","lobart's farm","lobart / hilda")),
        Quest("CH1-015",1,15,"Lobart's Concern",category="Lobart's Farm",giver = "Lobart",location="Lobart's Farm",prerequisites="Complete Harvesting Turnips.",summary="Ask Lobart what is worrying him, then investigate the strangers on the nearby plateau beyond the stone circle.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Ask Lobart what is worrying him, then investigate the strangers on the nearby plateau beyond the stone circle. You will find Brotherhood sect members cultivating swampweed. Speak with Shrat there, then return to Lobart and report what you found."),reward="100 XP for the investigation dialogue and 200 XP for reporting to Lobart.",warnings="If the field predators on the direct route are too strong, approach the plateau from the hill on the left instead of fighting them head-on.",searchTags=listOf("lobart's concern","lobart's farm","lobart")),
        Quest("CH1-016",1,16,"A Frying Pan for Hilda",category="Lobart's Farm",giver = "Hilda",location="Lobart's Farm",prerequisites="Complete Turnips for Hilda.",summary="Hilda gives you money to buy a frying pan.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Hilda gives you money to buy a frying pan. Canthar normally sells one beside Lobart's house; at night he is usually by the fireplace. Buy the pan and bring it to Hilda."),reward="150 XP and Hilda's meat soup, which grants +1 Strength.",warnings="Do not spend Hilda's money before securing the pan unless you can cover the purchase yourself.",searchTags=listOf("a frying pan for hilda","lobart's farm","hilda")),
        Quest("CH1-017",1,17,"For a Bottle of Wine",category="Lobart's Farm",giver = "Vino",location="Lobart's Farm",prerequisites="Chapter 1; Harvesting Turnips has begun.",summary="Vino asks for a bottle of wine.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Vino asks for a bottle of wine. Obtain one from Maleth by helping with the nearby bandits, steal/loot one from Lobart's farmhouse if you accept the consequences, or use another bottle you already own. Give Vino the wine."),reward="100 XP.",warnings="Using a legitimately obtained bottle avoids theft-related complications.",searchTags=listOf("for a bottle of wine","lobart's farm","vino")),
        Quest("CH1-018",1,18,"Bandits Near Lobart's Farm",category="Lobart's Farm",giver = "Maleth",location="Lobart's Farm",prerequisites="Chapter 1.",summary="Tell Maleth that bandits attacked you on the road.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Tell Maleth that bandits attacked you on the road. Go to the bandit cave where you meet Cavalorn and deal with the bandit situation there. If Jess is still alive, use the related Manhunt and Bandits dialogue before resolving his fate. Return to Maleth once the bandit threat has been dealt with."),reward="Experience and progress toward Lobart-farm rewards.",warnings="Jess connects to other early quests, so do not kill him immediately if you want the additional dialogue and rewards.",searchTags=listOf("bandits near lobart's farm","lobart's farm","maleth")),
        Quest("CH1-019",1,19,"Wine for Insomnia",category="Lobart's Farm",giver = "Vino",location="Lobart's Farm",prerequisites="Chapter 1; ask Vino for local news.",summary="Vino reports trouble keeping him awake.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Vino reports trouble keeping him awake. Search the low forest to the left of Khorinis's southern gate and kill the two orc scouts there. Loot the orc schnapps from them and return to Vino with the evidence."),reward="300 XP and a Goblin Berry.",warnings="The orcs can be dangerous at very low level; use terrain or return after gaining a few levels if necessary.",searchTags=listOf("wine for insomnia","lobart's farm","vino")),
        Quest("CH1-020",1,20,"The Man with the Eye Patch",category="Lobart's Farm",giver = "Greg",location="Lobart's Farm",prerequisites="Chapter 1; follow Greg's buried-treasure chain.",summary="Help Greg recover his hidden stashes around Khorinis.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Help Greg recover his hidden stashes around Khorinis. One stash is near the lake on the way toward the Valley of Mines pass and contains a silver cup; another is behind Bengar's barn and contains a gold goblet. Deliver the recovered valuables to Greg when he waits at the crossroads near Onar's and Sekob's farms. Continue his dialogue after learning Dexter's location and after the Dexter encounter."),reward="Gold and several staged XP rewards; the main treasure delivery awards 700 XP.",warnings="The quest can remain completable even if the Water Mage progression moves Greg, but it is cleaner to finish his Khorinis treasure sequence before leaving for Jharkendar.",searchTags=listOf("the man with the eye patch","lobart's farm","greg")),
        Quest("CH1-021",1,21,"Old Acquaintances",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Trigger quest",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1 onward; meet returning characters from Gothic I.",summary="Whenever you meet a returning Gothic I character, choose the dialogue that recognizes the person instead of pretending you do not remember them.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Whenever you meet a returning Gothic I character, choose the dialogue that recognizes the person instead of pretending you do not remember them. Valid encounters include Lester, Cavalorn, Shrat, Lares, Lee, Gorn, Saturas, Thorus, Huno, Milten, Diego, Ur-Shak and others. Keep speaking to old acquaintances as the story opens new locations."),reward="Usually 100 XP per recognized acquaintance; some characters give larger bonuses.",warnings="The recognition dialogue is the intended route for the bonus. Choosing amnesia-style responses forfeits the corresponding recognition reward.",searchTags=listOf("old acquaintances","khorinis island","automatic through gothic i acquaintances")),
        Quest("CH1-022",1,22,"Herbs for Constantino",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Lester",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; must be done before entering Khorinis by another route.",summary="Ask Lester how to get into Khorinis.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Ask Lester how to get into Khorinis. Collect 10 plants of the same accepted herb type, then approach the southern city gate and tell the guards the herbs are for Constantino. The guards let you in. Return to Lester afterward if his dialogue is still available."),reward="200 XP and +1 rhetoric at the gate; further XP is available by reporting to Lester.",warnings="MISSABLE: speaking with Lothar or entering the city by another route first can close this special herb-entry solution. You can combine it with the swimming route if you deliberately leave the city again before triggering Lothar.",searchTags=listOf("herbs for constantino","khorinis island","lester")),
        Quest("CH1-023",1,23,"Bandits and Cavalorn",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Cavalorn",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; before the Water Mage portal progression.",summary="Meet Cavalorn near the bandit cave and offer to help him.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Meet Cavalorn near the bandit cave and offer to help him. Before combat, speak to Jess at the cave entrance and warn him that Cavalorn is coming if you want to preserve Jess for his related quests. Kill the remaining bandits with Cavalorn or handle them yourself, then speak to Cavalorn again."),reward="250 XP, 50 gold and Cavalorn becomes available as a trainer.",warnings="Warning Jess keeps him alive for later dialogue and his mercenary-armor quest. If you send Jess deeper into the cave or start the fight carelessly, Cavalorn may kill him.",searchTags=listOf("bandits and cavalorn","khorinis island","cavalorn")),
        Quest("CH1-024",1,24,"Cavalorn's Old Shack",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Cavalorn",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; discuss traveling toward the Valley of Mines.",summary="Visit Cavalorn's old shack and search it thoroughly.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Visit Cavalorn's old shack and search it thoroughly. Take the leather pouch containing a piece of magic ore, then return to Cavalorn and tell him what you found. Give him the pouch/ore when the dialogue appears."),reward="1,000 XP for finding the shack and a further 300 XP plus 100 gold for returning the ore.",warnings="The quest may stay hidden depending on the dialogue route, but the hut can still be visited and the reward obtained.",searchTags=listOf("cavalorn's old shack","khorinis island","cavalorn")),
        Quest("CH1-025",1,25,"Manhunt and Bandits",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Jess / related bandit investigation",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; interact with Jess during the early bandit encounters.",summary="Question Jess about the bandits and Dexter rather than killing him immediately.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Question Jess about the bandits and Dexter rather than killing him immediately. Follow the leads toward Dexter's camp and use the information in the wider Missing People investigation. Resolve the bandit camp situation, then return to any NPCs whose dialogue remains open."),reward="Experience and information that advances the Dexter/Missing People chain.",warnings="If you first speak to Jess only after Dexter is already dead, the journal entry can linger until the next chapter even though the practical objective is finished.",searchTags=listOf("manhunt and bandits","khorinis island","jess / related bandit investigation")),
        Quest("CH1-026",1,26,"Mercenary Armor for Jess",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Jess",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Keep Jess alive during the Cavalorn/bandit encounter.",summary="After warning Jess about Cavalorn, speak with him again once he has moved away from immediate danger.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("After warning Jess about Cavalorn, speak with him again once he has moved away from immediate danger. Help him obtain mercenary-style armor through the dialogue/quest route he gives you, then return and hand it over."),reward="Experience and completion of Jess's early side story.",warnings="Use the warning that Cavalorn is very angry so Jess flees toward the forest. The wrong warning can send him deeper into the cave, where he may be killed.",searchTags=listOf("mercenary armor for jess","khorinis island","jess")),
        Quest("CH1-027",1,27,"The Missing",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Multiple NPCs during the missing-people investigation",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; tied to Where Are All the Missing People?",summary="Collect reports about missing residents across Khorinis and its farms.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Collect reports about missing residents across Khorinis and its farms. Important names include Tonak/Telbor, Pardos and Patrick; their relatives or employers point you toward the kidnappers. In Jharkendar, free the abducted people and complete Raven's Slaves, including dealing with Bloodwyn and the slave situation. Return to the original contacts in Khorinis to report who was found."),reward="Multiple XP/gold rewards for each rescued person and report-back stage.",warnings="Take the conversations in Khorinis before rushing through the bandit storyline; several of them open separate journal entries and reward stages.",searchTags=listOf("the missing","khorinis island","multiple npcs during the missing-people investigation")),
        Quest("CH1-028",1,28,"A Pirate's Trade",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Skip",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; before the first trip to Jharkendar.",summary="Speak with Skip on the beach north of Khorinis and discuss trade.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Speak with Skip on the beach north of Khorinis and discuss trade. Talk to Baltram in the marketplace and volunteer to act as courier. Carry Baltram's package to Skip, then return to Baltram after the delivery."),reward="XP, gold/rum, and a possible discount when entering the pirate camp.",warnings="If you keep the package until Chapter 2 and use it during the pirate-camp entry sequence, it can reduce the entry price by 100 gold. Delivering immediately gives a smaller immediate reward.",searchTags=listOf("a pirate's trade","khorinis island","skip")),
        Quest("CH1-029",1,29,"A New Weapon for Skip",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Skip",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; before first entering Jharkendar.",summary="Skip wants a new pirate saber.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Skip wants a new pirate saber. You can obtain one from the beach near the ship where a lizard guards the area, receive one through Sarah's Canthar-related outcome, or buy one from Sarah/Halvor depending on your game state. Bring the saber to Skip."),reward="250 XP and special rum that grants +1 Strength and +1 Dexterity.",warnings="Any valid pirate saber works; choose the route that fits your Canthar/Sarah decision.",searchTags=listOf("a new weapon for skip","khorinis island","skip")),
        Quest("CH1-030",1,30,"An Unexpected Meeting",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Trigger quest",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; complete earlier quests in the same area/faction if the dialogue is not yet available.",summary="Start this quest in Khorinis Island and exhaust the new dialogue connected with \"An Unexpected Meeting\".",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Start this quest in Khorinis Island and exhaust the new dialogue connected with \"An Unexpected Meeting\". Follow the dialogue chain for \"An Unexpected Meeting\" in Khorinis Island. Speak to the quest giver and every newly mentioned NPC, inspect the locations or objects added to the journal, and complete the objective that causes the journal to update. Return to the relevant giver/contact after each major update; if no new dialogue appears, complete earlier quests in the same area or faction and check again."),reward="Reward varies by quest/build; exact values should be taken from the current in-game dialogue or source page.",warnings="This is an index-guided quick solution. Exact item counts, coordinates and reward values can differ with New Balance updates; use the linked source record when a build-specific detail matters.",searchTags=listOf("an unexpected meeting","khorinis island","local quest giver in khorinis island")),
        Quest("CH1-031",1,31,"Becoming a Shaman",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Ur-Tarok",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; before Chapter 2. Find the peaceful shaman west of the forest north of Khorinis.",summary="Ask Akil about unusual activity to get a lead on Ur-Tarok, then find the peaceful orc shaman on the western edge of the northern forest.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Ask Akil about unusual activity to get a lead on Ur-Tarok, then find the peaceful orc shaman on the western edge of the northern forest. Speak with him and accept his shaman training tasks. The first collection requires shadowbeast hides, wolf skins and fangs; bring the requested trophies back, then continue every new training dialogue/task he offers."),reward="Subclass progression, staged XP and access to shaman abilities.",warnings="Do this before Chapter 2 if you want the shaman subclass path available as early as intended.",searchTags=listOf("becoming a shaman","khorinis island","ur-tarok")),
        Quest("CH1-032",1,32,"Hungry Convict",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Ragnar",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; before Chapter 3.",summary="Find Ragnar near the plateau with the burned houses off the road around the Dead Harpy region.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Find Ragnar near the plateau with the burned houses off the road around the Dead Harpy region. Speak with him and help the starving convict as requested. Search the nearby cave and surrounding plateau for the supplies/clues connected to his situation, then resolve his dialogue chain."),reward="Experience and access to later Ragnar content.",warnings="Ragnar has several dialogue outcomes that influence where he later goes and which follow-up quest path becomes available, so read the choices before committing.",searchTags=listOf("hungry convict","khorinis island","ragnar")),
        Quest("CH1-033",1,33,"Erol's Stinking Beast",category="Khorinis Island",giver = "Erol",location="Khorinis Island",prerequisites="Chapter 1; complete earlier quests in the same area/faction if the dialogue is not yet available.",summary="Start this quest in Khorinis Island and exhaust the new dialogue connected with \"Erol's Stinking Beast\".",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Start this quest in Khorinis Island and exhaust the new dialogue connected with \"Erol's Stinking Beast\". Follow the dialogue chain for \"Erol's Stinking Beast\" in Khorinis Island. Speak to the quest giver and every newly mentioned NPC, inspect the locations or objects added to the journal, and complete the objective that causes the journal to update. Return to the relevant giver/contact after each major update; if no new dialogue appears, complete earlier quests in the same area or faction and check again."),reward="Reward varies by quest/build; exact values should be taken from the current in-game dialogue or source page.",warnings="This is an index-guided quick solution. Exact item counts, coordinates and reward values can differ with New Balance updates; use the linked source record when a build-specific detail matters.",searchTags=listOf("erol's stinking beast","khorinis island","local quest giver in khorinis island")),
